WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.690
An ancient Hindu text describes
ultimate reality only by what it is not:

2
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.230
not this, not this.

3
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:14.120
Another says: there the eye does
not go, nor speech, nor mind.

4
00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:18.540
Yet many Hindus sing devotional
songs to a personal God of love,

5
00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.470
power and beauty.

6
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.010
Can one ultimate reality
be beyond all description,

7
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.730
and also a God you can love?

8
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:30.590
In this mission, you'll meet
Brahman, and 2 key words:

9
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.940
nirguna and saguna.

10
00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:36.870
Then you'll weigh up whether Brahman
is best understood without qualities,

11
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.280
or with them.

12
00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:43.700
Your mission: find out whether one ultimate
reality can be beyond all description

13
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.870
and also a God you can love.
